### Page 1 of 5

```text
Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO
To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Seth Lloyd, AICP
Subject: Planning Commission Petition for a Zoning Map Amendment
Date:
October 28, 2024

Background:
The item for consideration is a petition for a Zoning Map Amendment (zone change). The UDC allows
the Planning Commission to petition the Governing Body to make a Zoning Map Amendment in
Subsection 2.2.1.b.2.

At their regular meeting on October 7, 2024, the Planning Commission had an applicant requesting the
UU Urban Use Overlay zone be added to their parcel. The Planning Commission discussed the merits of
applying the UU to one parcel, and eventually recommended approval with a one-vote margin. At the
end of the meeting, under other business, the Planning Commission discussed the option of expanding
the UU to a larger area for a more robust district. The Planning Commission was informed of their ability
to petition the Governing Body. At their regular meeting on October 21, 2024, the Planning Commission
made a formal motion to petition. The petition is attached.

The petition requests changing the zoning of the block face along the east side of Warren between 21st
Street and 22nd Street from MUR Mixed-Use Residential to MUR Mixed-Use Residential with UU Urban
Use Overlay. A map of the area is below, and the legal description is in the attached petition.

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
```

### Page 2 of 5

```text
To proceed with a formal Zoning Map Amendment, the petition needs accepted by the Governing Body,
which will direct Staff to initiate the Zoning Map Amendment process, including legal notice, posted
notice, mailed notice, a Planning Commission Public Hearing, and the drafting of the Zoning Map
Amendment Ordinance.

The proposed Governing Body review schedule for the Resolution is as follows:
•
Introduction and Referral
October 28, 2024
•
Public Services Committee
November 5, 2024
•
Final consideration

November 12, 2024
A separate Ordinance would be brought forward after the Resolution is approved.

Attachments:
1. Resolution
```

### Page 3 of 5

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION ACKNOWLEDGING RECEIPT OF A PETITION BY
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE PLANNING COMMISSION TO ADD THE UU
URBAN USE OVERLAY TO AN AREA ZONED MUR MIXED-USE
RESIDENTIAL EMPHASIS WITH FRONTAGE ON THE EAST SIDE OF
WARREN AVENUE BETWEEN 21ST AND 22ND STREETS AND
DIRECTING STAFF TO INITIATE A ZONING MAP AMENDMENT
PURSUANT TO THE PETITION."

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission (Planning Commission) held a
regularly scheduled Public Meeting on October 7, 2024 and while discussing an agenda item,
signaled the need for and the Planning Commission’s support of a UU Urban Use Overlay in
several areas of throughout the community;

WHEREAS, 2.2.1(b)(2) of the Unified Development Code allows for the Planning
Commission to petition the Governing Body for a zoning map amendment;

WHEREAS, at its October 7, 2024 meeting, the Planning Commission was specifically
concerned about parcels of property in an area zoned MUR Mixed-Use Residential Emphasis with
frontage on the east side of Warren Avenue between 21st and 22nd Streets;

WHEREAS, the legal description of the property area at issue is: legally described as: the
south ½ of Lot 3, the west 9’ of the north ½ of Lot 3, Lot 4, and Lot 5, Block 234, Original City,
Cheyenne, Wyoming;

WHEREAS, at its October 21, 2024 meeting, the Planning Commission voted to petition
the Governing Body for a zoning map amendment to add the UU Overlay to the parcels of property
in an area zoned MUR Mixed-Use Residential Emphasis with frontage on the east side of Warren
Avenue between 21st and 22nd Street; and

WHEREAS, immediately following the October 21, 2024 meeting, the Chair of the
Planning Commission signed a Petition requesting that the Governing Body add the UU Urban
Use Overlay to an area zoned MUR Mixed-Use Residential Emphasis with frontage on the east
side of Warren Avenue between 21st and 22nd Streets (attached and incorporated herein as Exhibit
A).

NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Governing Body acknowledges receipt of the petition by
the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission to add the UU Urban Use Overlay in an area zoned
MUR Mixed-Use Residential Emphasis with frontage on the east side of Warren Avenue between
21st and 22nd Streets;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that staff of the Planning and Development Department
are directed to draft an amendment to the Unified Development Code to add the UU Urban Use
Overlay in an area zoned MUR Mixed-Use Residential Emphasis with frontage on the east side of
11:30 am, Oct 23 2024
